mise-download-url-replacements

From: Victor Araújo <victor@victor-software-house.com>

Downstream-Reason: Download mise, its signed checksums and its packslip through the MISE_URL_REPLACEMENTS rules that mise itself honors, so CI fetches everything through one mirror. Plain keys follow mise's rule: in order, every occurrence, first rule that yields a different valid URL wins; regex: keys are skipped. Credentials in a rewritten URL reach curl on stdin, never argv, and a failed mirror download falls back to the original URL.
Upstream-Status: not-submitted
Drop-When: Upstream jdx/mise-action applies MISE_URL_REPLACEMENTS to its own downloads with credentials kept off the command line.
---
 .github/workflows/test.yml        |   38 +++++
 README.md                         |   19 +++
 dist/index.js                     |  Bin
 dist/index.js.map                 |  Bin
 scripts/url-replacements.test.mjs |  273 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/index.ts                      |  101 ++++++++++----
 src/url-replacements.ts           |  123 +++++++++++++++++
 7 files changed, 529 insertions(+), 25 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 scripts/url-replacements.test.mjs
 create mode 100644 src/url-replacements.ts

diff --git a/.github/workflows/test.yml b/.github/workflows/test.yml
index 439e36a1e3a6512e99fd769a0a3fbe02abcfa209..6051ac07109afc8c1910ef33e9df32ecd92b2836 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/test.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/test.yml
@@ -489,6 +489,44 @@ jobs:
         shell: bash
         run: test "$(cat "$MISE_ACTION_CURL_ATTEMPTS")" = 3
 
+  url_replacements:
+    timeout-minutes: 10
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    steps:
+      - uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7.0.1
+        with:
+          persist-credentials: false
+      - name: Record curl command lines
+        shell: bash
+        run: |
+          real_curl="$(command -v curl)"
+          mock_bin="$RUNNER_TEMP/mock-bin"
+          mkdir -p "$mock_bin"
+          cat > "$mock_bin/curl" <<EOF
+          #!/usr/bin/env bash
+          printf '%s\n' "\$*" >> "\$MISE_ACTION_CURL_LOG"
+          exec "$real_curl" "\$@"
+          EOF
+          chmod +x "$mock_bin/curl"
+          echo "$mock_bin" >> "$GITHUB_PATH"
+          echo "MISE_ACTION_CURL_LOG=$RUNNER_TEMP/curl-log" >> "$GITHUB_ENV"
+      - name: Setup mise through an unreachable mirror
+        uses: $/
+        env:
+          MISE_URL_REPLACEMENTS: '{"https://github.com/": "https://ci:url-replacements-test-secret@mirror.invalid/github/"}'
+        with:
+          cache: false
+          install: false
+          mise_dir: ${{ runner.temp }}/mise-url-replacements
+          version: 2026.11.5
+      - run: mise --version
+      - name: Check the mirror was tried without credentials on the command line
+        shell: bash
+        run: |
+          grep -q 'https://mirror.invalid/github/jdx/mise/releases/download/v2026.11.5/mise-v2026.11.5-' "$MISE_ACTION_CURL_LOG"
+          grep -q 'https://mirror.invalid/github/jdx/mise/releases/download/v2026.11.5/packslip.sigstore.json' "$MISE_ACTION_CURL_LOG"
+          ! grep -q 'url-replacements-test-secret' "$MISE_ACTION_CURL_LOG"
+
   test-typescript:
     timeout-minutes: 10
     name: TypeScript Tests
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 136999028bdb5b9d4383e1158d7cdc79e13f6d41..fb7cecf5cd25fdc614ce3529506cec41bb33cc72 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -393,6 +393,25 @@ When a repo mise lock file is present, the action automatically runs
 `bootstrap: true`; use `bootstrap_skip` and `bootstrap_args` for bootstrap
 customization.
 
+## Download mise through a mirror
+
+The action downloads mise, its signed checksums and its packslip through the
+[`MISE_URL_REPLACEMENTS`](https://mise.jdx.dev/url-replacements.html) rules
+that mise itself uses, so one setting routes both through the mirror:
+
+```yaml
+- uses: jdx/mise-action@v4
+  env:
+    MISE_URL_REPLACEMENTS: '{"https://github.com/": "https://mirror.example.com/github/"}'
+```
+
+The action applies plain keys as mise does and skips `regex:` keys. Every
+download is still verified against mise's signatures. Credentials in a
+replacement URL are masked in the log and passed to curl on stdin, never on its
+command line, so they need curl on the runner. When a download through the
+mirror fails after one retry, the action warns and downloads from the original
+URL with the full retry policy.
+
 ## Alternative Installation
 
 Alternatively, mise is easy to use in GitHub Actions even without this:
